      "questionName": "native speaker, second language, first language, standard",
      "questionType": "FillBlank",
      "questionText": "<p><strong>Read the conversation and then choose the correct answer to fill in each blank.</strong></p>\n<p>Nga: Hi, Quang! I was reading about World Englishes and got curious. Do you know what a <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>14.1</label><select class='ms fillblank-option-14' index='0' name='fbo-906075-0' data-testid='fillblank-select-906075-0'><option value='' data-testid='fillblank-option-empty-906075-0'></option><option value=\"public\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-0-public'>public</option><option value=\"native\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-0-native'>native</option></select></span></strong> speaker of English is?</p>\n<p>Quang: Yes, it is someone who speaks English as their <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>14.2</label><select class='ms fillblank-option-14' index='1' name='fbo-906075-1' data-testid='fillblank-select-906075-1'><option value='' data-testid='fillblank-option-empty-906075-1'></option><option value=\"first\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-1-first'>first</option><option value=\"foreign\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-1-foreign'>foreign</option></select></span></strong>&nbsp;language, like people from the UK or the US.</p>\n<p>Nga: That makes sense! What about people who speak English as a <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>14.3</label><select class='ms fillblank-option-14' index='2' name='fbo-906075-2' data-testid='fillblank-select-906075-2'><option value='' data-testid='fillblank-option-empty-906075-2'></option><option value=\"written\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-2-written'>written</option><option value=\"second\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-2-second'>second</option></select></span> </strong>language?</p>\n<p>Quang: Well, many people around the world speak English to connect with others or for work, not because it is their mother tongue. It&#8217;s common in countries like India or Singapore.</p>\n<p>Nga: Interesting! Is there any <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>14.4</label><select class='ms fillblank-option-14' index='3' name='fbo-906075-3' data-testid='fillblank-select-906075-3'><option value='' data-testid='fillblank-option-empty-906075-3'></option><option value=\"standard\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-3-standard'>standard</option><option value=\"degree\" data-testid='fillblank-option-906075-3-degree'>degree</option></select></span></strong> in English?</p>\n<p>Quang: Yes, there are certain rules for grammar and pronunciation, but English can be different in various countries.</p>",
